The read-only root of an image-based system (composefs, an overlay mounted
on /) holds no user files, yet Solid lists it as a storage device. Every path
then falls under it: /home is a symlink to /var/home and Solid compares paths
without resolving symlinks, so Dolphin's status bar asks the overlay for free
space and shows "0 B free". Without the overlay the caller uses the path
itself, which finds the real disk.

--- a/src/solid/devices/frontend/devicemanager.cpp
+++ b/src/solid/devices/frontend/devicemanager.cpp
@@ -163,6 +163,10 @@ Solid::Device Solid::Device::storageAccessFromPath(const QString &path)
 
         QString mountPath = storageAccess->filePath();
 
+        if (mountPath == QLatin1String("/") && device.udi().startsWith(QLatin1String("/org/kde/fstab/overlay"))) {
+            continue;
+        }
+
         if (mountPath.size() <= match_length || !path.startsWith(mountPath)) {
             continue;
         }
